Reconstruct FUN_1000_3a14 (joystick calibration) and its callee FUN_1000_3ebf (SMC far-JMP-thunk
linked-list insert) faithfully from asm. Class: folded do{}while(true) infinite-loop (3a14) +
host-deref of a DGROUP near-ptr / far-ptr list (3ebf, same family as patch 012).

FUN_1000_3a14 asm (base-0 0x13a14):
  xor bx,bx; mov si,0x200; lcall [DGROUP:0x12]   ; BX=0 => far reloc-applier f842 bails (no-op)
  movw [0x1e1e],0 ; movb [0x300],0
  mov ax,[0x44e]; L: cmp [0x44e],ax; je L         ; wait one PIT tick (DGROUP:0x44e, incw at ISR 0x131c4)
  mov bx,[0x44e]; xor cx,cx; mov dx,0x201
  L2: in al,dx; inc cx; je done; cmp [0x44e],bx; je L2
  done: dec cx; mov [0x1e1a],cx                    ; count of joystick-port reads within one tick
  mov al,8;  lcall [0x2d4]                          ; device method (al=8)
  mov al,0xff; lcall [0x2d8]                        ; device method (al=0xff)
  mov bx,0x1e20; L3: movw [bx],0xffff; add bx,0xb; cmp bx,0x1e78; jb L3   ; init the 8x 11-byte table
  mov cx,cs; mov dx,0x4c19; mov bx,0x2ec; call 3ebf(cs,0x4c19,0x2ec)      ; register the poll thunk
  movb [0x301],0xff; clc; lret

Ghidra saw the tick-spin (mov ax,[0x44e]; cmp [0x44e],ax; je) as an infinite loop and folded the
ENTIRE body to `(*DAT_c012)(); do{}while(true);` (six "Removing unreachable block" warnings). The
spin is the same volatile-ISR-flag class as patch 017: DGROUP:0x44e is the PIT tick counter the
INT-8 ISR advances (asm 0x131c4 `incw [0x44e]`). Reconstruct both spins as genuine volatile re-reads
that cooperatively pump the timer (fist_timer_pump). The 0x201 read loop counts reads-per-tick as a
CPU-speed baseline for later polling; with NO joystick present port 0x201 reads the no-joystick value
(0xf0 -- buttons high, axis one-shots low; fist_vga.c), which this loop does not inspect -- it
terminates when the tick advances (in() pumps the timer) or cx wraps (timeout). So calibration BAILS
(returns) instead of waiting forever, matching the original's no-joystick path.

FUN_1000_3ebf asm (base-0 0x13ebf): inserts a far-JMP-thunk node into a linked list.
  param_1 (cx) = new node SEGMENT; param_2 (dx) = new node OFFSET;
  param_3 (bx) = NEAR offset into DGROUP of the list-head far pointer.
  head far-ptr at DGROUP:param_3 -> node; nodes are 5-byte thunks (byte[0]=0xeb jmp opcode,
  bytes[3..4]=link off, bytes[5..6]=link seg). If the head node is a thunk, walk to the last thunk
  and insert the new node after it (new node inherits the old link); else head-insert.
Ghidra host-deref'd param_3 (0x2ec) and every far link as host pointers (-> SIGSEGV). Reconstructed
memory-faithfully via g_mem+(seg<<4)+off. The thunk nodes live in the SMC scratch region and are
inert for our C control flow (we never execute g_mem as code) but the list is kept byte-exact.
